 *     finish to stand out: built-in wardrobe guide, "Presence".
 *   - Floating or framed shelving over cupboards: alcove guide, "Layout"; his
 *     20 Oct email ("floating or framed shelving").
 *   - Shelf openings of around 250 to 350 mm for books and 350 to 450 mm or
 *     more for larger display pieces: facts table (alcove shelf openings,
 *     14 Oct); alcove guide, "Depth and spacing".
 *   - Wardrobes either side of the bed with bedside shelves or drawers;
 *     cupboards above the headboard for less used things, spare bedding,
 *     out-of-season clothes: built-in wardrobe guide, "Storage around the
 *     bed" and "Storage". The height above the mattress is his to give: the
 *     <Ask> "maida-vale-over-bed-clearance".
 *   - Shaker or handleless doors in mansion flats: his Hampstead text (10 Nov).
 *   - Check the listing on Westminster's listed buildings page, whose listed
 *     building map searches by street: that page, read 26 Nov 2026 (S5). Ask
 *     the council before work starts, especially for original skirting or
 *     panelling: facts table (listed homes row, 26 Nov Islington).
 *   - Agree where to unload and park before fitting day: facts table (8 and
 *     10 Nov Hampstead, 23 Nov Camden). Who applies for a Westminster trade
